    19	\begin{lemma}
    20	\label{lem:P4algo}
    21	There is an algorithm that determines if $G$ is $k$-contractible to a path of at most five vertices with the first witness set containing $X$ and the last witness set containing $Y$ in $\mathcal{O}^*(2^{k-|X|-|Y|})$ time. 
    22	\end{lemma}
    23	\begin{proof}
    24	%\todo{K:toedit}
    25	If $G$ is $k$-contractible to a path of at most five vertices 
    26	then $n \leq k+5$ by Observation~\ref{obs:sumofws-path}. Thus, if $n 
    27	>k+5$, then we declare that $G$ is not $k$-contractible to a path on at 
    28	most five vertices. Subsequently, we assume $n \leq k+5$. Suppose $G$ is $k$-contractible to a path $P_{\ell}$ for some $2 \le \ell \le 5$, and $(W_1,\dots, W_{\ell})$ is the corresponding path
    29	witness structure. Consider a $2$-coloring of $V(G)$ such that every witness set is monochromatic and the adjacent witness sets get different colors.
    30	In such a coloring, the first and the last witness set get the same color
    31	when $\ell$ is odd and different colors when $\ell$ is even.
    32	We consider these two cases seperately.
    33	
    34	We first compute the set of all colorings of $V(G)$ using two colors such that $X$ and $Y$ are monochromatic and have the same color. 
    35	Then, we iterate over this set, contract each of the connected 
    36	components of the two monochromatic subgraphs into a single vertex and 
    37	check if the resultant graph is a path with first witness set 
    38	containing $X$ and the last witness set containing $Y$ and at most $k$ edges were contracted. 
    39	We repeat this procedure with the set of all colorings of $V(G)$ using two colors such that $X$ and $Y$ are monochromatic but have different colors.
    40	If no coloring results in the required $P_\ell$ with $\ell \leq 5$, then $G$ is 
    41	not $k$-contractible to a path of at most five vertices with first witness set 
    42	containing $X$ and the last witness set containing $Y$. Otherwise, we obtain 
    43	a $P_\ell$ from $G$ using at most $k$ edge contractions with witness structure 
    44	$(W_1,W_2,\ldots,W_\ell)$ 
    45	where $\ell \leq 5$ and $X \subseteq W_1$, $Y 
    46	\subseteq W_\ell$.  
    47	
    48	As there are $\mathcal{O}(2^{k+5-|X|-|Y|}$ such colorings, the overall 
    49	running time of this algorithm is $\mathcal{O}^*(2^{k-|X|-|Y|})$. \qed
