Find endpoint certificates for path contractions in a chordal split graph.

The graph G is defined as follows.  X={x0,...,x4} and
Y={y0,...,y4} are independent sets.  Z={zX,z0,...,z5,zY} is a
clique.  Vertex xi is adjacent to zX and to coordinate vertex zc exactly when
bit c of its displayed row is 1.  Vertex yj is adjacent to zY and to zc exactly
when bit c of its row is 1.  There are no other edges.  Thus G is a connected
chordal split graph.  Every row has exactly 3 one-bits.

For a proposed pair [i,j], define Z1 as the neighbors of xi in Z, Z2 as the
neighbors of yj in Z, and Z3=Z\(Z1 union Z2).  The pair is valid exactly when
the following four nonempty bags form a path-witness structure in the listed
order:
  W1={xi}
  W2=Z1 union Z3 union (X\{xi})
  W3=Z2 union (Y\{yj})
  W4={yj}
A path-witness structure means that every bag induces a connected subgraph,
the bags partition all vertices, and two distinct bags have at least one edge
between them exactly when they are consecutive in the displayed order.  Such a
structure contracts G to the four-vertex path P4 using exactly k=14
edge contractions.

Return exactly 2 distinct valid pairs.  Indices are 0-based and lie in
0..4.  Order within a pair is always [X-index,Y-index].  Sort the list of
pairs lexicographically; repeats are forbidden.

X rows (left-to-right bits correspond to z0,...,z5):
  x0: 010011
  x1: 001110
  x2: 100011
  x3: 100110
  x4: 011010

Y rows (left-to-right bits correspond to z0,...,z5):
  y0: 010110
  y1: 010101
  y2: 110001
  y3: 011001
  y4: 000111

Give your final answer inside <answer></answer> tags as a JSON list of 2
integer pairs sorted lexicographically.
Example format: <answer>[[0,3],[4,1]]</answer>
Output nothing else inside the tags.
