codex
A second audit against Section 5.2 confirms the exact reduction details and the paper’s caveat that the fine-grained lower bound is meaningful for sparse inputs. I also removed an accidental leak from the statement: it no longer announces that every row has equal Hamming weight; that fact is now something to notice (or receive through the structural hint), while all definitions needed to grade remain explicit. The compact graph specification stays sparse in the reduction’s incidence representation.
