+This cannot honestly be Track A. The paper gives an `O*(2^k)` general algorithm
+(Theorem 1), cites an `O(nm)` chordal-graph algorithm immediately before
+Theorem 4, and the visible source instance can always be solved by scanning all
+`n^2` Boolean-vector pairs in `O(n^2 d)` time. At the hard preset that exact
+reference scan succeeds on 8/8 instances, performs 640,000 Boolean coordinate
+products per instance, and takes 0.086 seconds per instance in the recorded run.
 
-The compact route uses the extra distributional structure: because every row has
