+Generation is inverse. It samples the endpoint vectors first, samples each
+designated mate inside the endpoint's complement, and then adds only rows that
+intersect every opposite-side row. Non-endpoint rows occur in pairs under the
+coordinate-half swap. The local rejection tests prevent extra solutions; they
+do not discover the already-chosen certificate. All rows have the same Hamming
+weight, and planted and decoy rows have the same one-row marginal language.
 
