+An instance here asks for all of a fixed number of endpoint pairs. Each pair
+deterministically expands to the proof's four bags. `verify` checks exact support
+disjointness, constructs the graph, checks the partition, runs connectivity
+searches inside every bag, checks all six quotient adjacencies against `P4`, and
+checks the contraction budget. It never reads `inst["answer"]`.
+
+Generation is inverse. It samples the endpoint vectors first, samples each
+designated mate inside the endpoint's complement, and then adds only rows that
+intersect every opposite-side row. Non-endpoint rows occur in pairs under the
+coordinate-half swap. The local rejection tests prevent extra solutions; they
+do not discover the already-chosen certificate. All rows have the same Hamming
+weight, and planted and decoy rows have the same one-row marginal language.
 
 ## Why Track B
 
-This cannot honestly be Track A.  The paper itself gives an
-`O*(2^k)` Path Contraction algorithm (Theorem 1), quotes an `O(nm)` algorithm on
-chordal graphs immediately before Theorem 4, and its reduction exposes the
-standard `O(n²d)` Orthogonal Vectors scan.  At the hard preset the measured
-reference scan succeeds on 8/8 instances, performs 202,752 coordinate products,
-and averages 0.0382 seconds on this host.
+This cannot honestly be Track A. The paper gives an `O*(2^k)` general algorithm
+(Theorem 1), cites an `O(nm)` chordal-graph algorithm immediately before
+Theorem 4, and the visible source instance can always be solved by scanning all
+`n^2` Boolean-vector pairs in `O(n^2 d)` time. At the hard preset that exact
+reference scan succeeds on 8/8 instances, performs 640,000 Boolean coordinate
+products per instance, and takes 0.086 seconds per instance in the recorded run.
 
-The compact route uses the extra distributional structure: because every row has
-weight `d/2`, disjoint rows are full bitwise complements.  Complement lookup costs
-`2n+t = 200` high-level exact operations at the hard preset, within the no-tool
-cap but onerous across 192 shuffled bit strings.  This algorithm is disclosed,
-not placed among the failing attacks.  The hardening experiment needed to show
-that models actually experience that gap is still missing because of the API
-quota.
+The compact route notices that swapping the low and high 32-coordinate halves
+is an involution. Every decoy row has its swapped mate on the same side; only the
+four endpoint rows do not. Two hash-membership passes isolate those rows, after
+which only their 4-by-4 cross-product is tested. This is 216 exact word
+operations. Without the symmetry, the solver faces 10,000 shuffled cross-pairs.
 
-Easy regimes deliberately avoided are target `P3` (polynomial time, Introduction),
