+An instance here asks for all of a fixed number of endpoint pairs. Each pair
+deterministically expands to the proof's four bags. `verify` checks exact support
+disjointness, constructs the graph, checks the partition, runs connectivity
+searches inside every bag, checks all six quotient adjacencies against `P4`, and
+checks the contraction budget. It never reads `inst["answer"]`.
+
+Generation is inverse. It samples the endpoint vectors first, samples each
+designated mate inside the endpoint's complement, and then adds only rows that
+intersect every opposite-side row. Non-endpoint rows occur in pairs under the
+coordinate-half swap. The local rejection tests prevent extra solutions; they
