The family uses the paper’s Section 5.2/Theorem 4 reduction from Orthogonal Vectors to four-bag path-contraction witnesses. It inverse-generates four endpoint certificates and verifies their complete graph partitions exactly.

Local results:

- G1–G8 pass.
- Structured guessing: 0/200,000; exact density \(2.40\times10^{-15}\).
- Reference scan: 640,000 Boolean operations, 8/8 solved.
- Compact half-swap route: 216 operations, 8/8 solved.
- Four failing attacks: 0/8 each.
- Answer: 40 characters, 8 atoms.
- G9 remains failed/pending.

All three oracle runs received HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded (total limit)`, so no model responses were scored. `submit.sh` correctly refuses submission on G9. This is not a paper rejection; once `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` is replenished, the bare and two G9 runs must be repeated. The family choice follows the full [arXiv paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.06290), including its polynomial/FPT easy regimes.
