+Contraction*](https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.06290) define an `H`-witness structure
+in Section 2 as a partition into nonempty connected bags whose quotient is
+exactly `H`. In the forward proof of Theorem 4, an orthogonal pair `x_i,y_j`
+in the reduction's Boolean-vector instance gives four explicit bags forming a
+`P4` witness structure of the constructed split graph.
 
-An instance here asks for a fixed number of distinct endpoint pairs.  Each pair
-deterministically expands to those four proof bags.  `verify` checks exact
