     5	%\defproblem{\textsc{Path Contraction With Constrained Ends}}{A connected graph $G$, two disjoint subsets $X,Y \subseteq V(G)$ and an integer $k$.}{Can one contract at most $k$ edges in $G$ to obtain a path with witness structure $(W_1,\ldots,W_\ell)$ such that $X \subseteq W_1$ and $Y \subseteq W_\ell$?} %Does $G$ have a path witness structure $(W_1,\ldots,W_\ell)$ such that $X \subseteq W_1$, $Y \subseteq W_\ell$ and $\underset{i \in [\ell]} \sum |W_i| \leq k+\ell$ for some $\ell \in \mathbb{N}^+$
