%Informally, we call a set $A$ as an $(S_X,W)$-attachment if $A$ can be appended as a new witness set to the path witness structure of $G[S_X]$ 
%that contains $W$ as the last witness set to obtain a path witness structure of $G[S_X \cup A]$.
