codex
The implementation and local audit are complete: all nine local gates pass, the hard preset is deterministic and hint-free by default, and 200 additional generated instances matched the exact solution set. The sole unresolved requirement is external: every revised bare, structural, and placebo oracle call received the same OpenRouter total-quota 403, so there is no valid STEP 4 hardness verdict to claim. I’m leaving the result explicitly marked “not ready to ship,” rather than treating API errors as model failures or rejecting the paper.
Implementation, local gates, reports, and documentation are complete. Mandatory oracle hardening remains pending because all live redraws are rejected by OpenRouter's exhausted total quota; errors were recorded and were not counted as failures.
  ✓ Read the full paper and identify exact definitions, hardness/easy regimes, and certificate algorithms
  ✓ Inspect repository harness and choose or reject one admissible family
  ✓ Implement generator, verifier, attacks, canonicalization, and self-test
  • Run gates, hardening loop, and G9 arms; adjust only as allowed
  ✓ Write reports and README, then verify deliverables
