codex
Implemented and locally verified a Track B generator based on the paper’s Theorem 4 Orthogonal Vectors reduction to chordal \(P_4\)-contraction. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2403.06290v1)

Key results:

- All G1–G9 local gates pass.
- G4: 0/200,000 guesses; exact density \(1/3{,}397{,}671{,}432{,}817{,}025\).
- G6: four attacks failed across 8/8 seeds.
- Reference scan: 1,081,600 coordinate products, 0.18 seconds.
- Compact symmetry route: 276 operations.
- A former \(n=40\) rung was solved by an oracle and removed.
- The current hard preset is \(n=130,d=64\).

Files:

- [gen_2403_06290.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2403.06290/gen_2403_06290.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2403.06290/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2403.06290/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2403.06290/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2403.06290/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2403.06290/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The result is not yet shippable: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded (total limit)” for every revised hardening and G9 redraw. These errors were correctly not counted as oracle failures. No `REJECTED.md` was created because this is an infrastructure block, not a failure of G, H, or V.
